# Contents list

A contents list gives a short route to sections within a long page or to chapters in a guide. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/content-list/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Use the shared navigation contract

[Contents list](../../components/contents-list.html#choose-the-navigation-scope) owns the distinction between “On this page” fragments and “In this guide” routes. This publishing source page retains its article examples. Use the [mini-hub pattern](../../patterns/mini-hub.html) when several real pages also need current-topic and previous/next context.

## When to use it

Use it on substantial installation, recovery or maintenance guidance. Write section names that describe the user task. Reduce unnecessary sections before adding more navigation. A three-sentence card does not need its own contents list.

## Structure and behaviour

Generate links from stable heading IDs and keep their order the same as the document. Label the navigation "On this page" for local anchors and "In this guide" for other pages. A current chapter is plain text. One nested level may help a technical guide; deeper nesting is a sign to restructure.

## Home Assistant boundary

The local contents list is a documentation pattern, not an injection into every HA panel. Sticky positioning must not hide the target under the header or consume the whole mobile viewport. Do not make a table of contents look like a progress checklist.

